  "result_text": "`GET /stats/monthly?year=&month=` is in place and returns the four counts and the late-fee total you specified. The build passes, the 4 new integration tests pass, and the 7 architecture tests pass. I committed the change to `feat/loan-limit` as `f9c2fd8`.\n\n- **Counting rules:** `loanCount` counts loans whose `loanedAt` falls in the month. `returnCount`, `overdueCount` and `lateFeeTotal` count loans whose `returnedAt` falls in the month. An overdue return is one with a late fee above 0. A month with no activity returns all zeros.\n- **Bad input:** a month outside 1–12 returns `400`. A year outside `Year.MIN_VALUE`–`Year.MAX_VALUE` also returns `400`.\n- **Structure:** this follows the hexagonal layout in CLAUDE.md. It adds a use case and a service, two new load methods on `LoadLoanPort`, the matching JPA queries, and a `StatsController` that returns a `MonthlyStatsResponse` record.\n- **Tests:** `MonthlyStatsIntegrationTest` covers a loan in one month returned late in the next, an on-time return, an empty month, and an out-of-range month. Each test uses its own month in 2031 so the shared H2 database can't mix in data from other tests.\n\nThe service loads every matching loan into memory and counts them in Java. That's simple and fine at library scale, but it would need count queries if monthly volume grows a lot.",
